ReadyNow Privacy Policy
Effective: 1 October 2026 · App: ReadyNow: Offline First Aid (com.readynow.app) · Developer: integrated apps for life

العربية
Summary
ReadyNow has no account and no server. Your emergency contacts and Medical IDs are stored only on your phone. The free version shows ads from Google AdMob, which collects some device data as described below. ReadyNow Pro removes ads and the ads SDK is then never started.

Information stored on your device only
Data	Why	Leaves your phone?
Emergency contacts (name, phone number)	To prepare your SOS message	Only when you send a message yourself through your SMS or messaging app
Medical IDs (name, blood type, allergies, conditions, medications, notes)	To show rescuers; blood type and allergies are added to your SOS message	Only inside a message you choose to send
Precise location (GPS)	Shown on the SOS screen and added to your SOS message	Only inside a message you choose to send. ReadyNow never uploads it.
Settings (language, country, Pro status)	App preferences	No
Location is read only while the SOS screen is open and only with your permission. You can deny it and still use every other feature.

Advertising (free version)
The free version uses the Google Mobile Ads SDK (AdMob). Google may collect: your device's advertising ID and app set ID, IP address (which gives an approximate location), ad interactions, and diagnostic/crash information, to show and measure ads, prevent fraud, and for analytics. If you are in a region that requires it (such as the EEA, UK or certain US states), you are asked for consent first, and you can change your choice anytime in Settings → Ad privacy choices. You can also reset or delete your advertising ID in your phone's Google settings.

Learn how Google uses data: policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites.

Purchases
ReadyNow Pro is sold through Google Play. Payment is handled entirely by Google; we never see your payment details. The app keeps only a local note that Pro is active. See the Google Privacy Policy.

Contact picker
When you choose "Pick from phone", Android gives ReadyNow access only to the single contact you pick. ReadyNow does not read your contact list.

Children
ReadyNow is not directed at children under 13 and we do not knowingly collect their data.

Deleting your data
Delete contacts and Medical IDs inside the app, or remove everything by uninstalling ReadyNow or using Settings → Apps → ReadyNow → Storage → Clear storage. We hold no copy on any server.

Security
Data is stored in the app's private storage, which other apps cannot read. Data the ads SDK sends is encrypted in transit.

Medical disclaimer
ReadyNow provides general first-aid guidance and does not replace professional medical help. In an emergency, call your local emergency number first.

Changes
We will update this page and its effective date when the app's data practices change.

